    {
      "question": "q-345034",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "6b1c5a4df019cf63a486701dacf8691bc1c64ef0f1f08ec7aca997d0f4795848",
      "new_sha256": "39d80b5435447303d6232e026084dc26afe71593105bcc5b29a264e122a5985f",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-345034",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4x+8)$ between $x=-2$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{5}{n}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061($\n\n{{field-1}}$)$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "2cf848a7d49b9b9bdee6211b328aa8a534a5b2ab12d7e1b0a95ac0c6f5182eb4"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2822,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 2823
    },
    {
      "question": "q-345034",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "2569a7247b2aa98ba315f57974ef4c3bd395ace7cd8905781aa59f8766ec3f48",
      "new_sha256": "18d6c04ee0f988c47b12eff43d4e4536698b1d1a27bd5119aa63a05ffa40e461",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-345034",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\u0394x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+j\u0394x$, and  $\u0394x=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=3,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\n\u0394x=\\frac{3-(-2)}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\u0394x & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+j\u0394x)\u0394x \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-2+j\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4(-2+\\frac{5j}{n})+8) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{20j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "2cf848a7d49b9b9bdee6211b328aa8a534a5b2ab12d7e1b0a95ac0c6f5182eb4"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2822,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 2823
    },
