    {
      "question": "e-401",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "d803c5af94c42d7ce50c7afdc6141fe77705d9eff2c9ea644886d20a265fbaa0",
      "new_sha256": "8b6d12cbe692066fe6538375acc417acc4d0b8d731102a22efe008d0dd3113a4",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-401",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} f(x_k)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_k = a + k\\Delta x$ with $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{2-(-1)}{3} = \\dfrac 3 3 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\u0394x & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+k\u0394x)\u0394x \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3-1}f(-1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}f(k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-(k-1)^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-{k}^{2}+2k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(3+2k-{k}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/example-401.json",
          "file_sha256": "494ce76718574d6fd87a036ac946075163d1a8aab7fa06987354ce6e8b4c965a"
        }
